# Optional portable calculation boundary — implementation evidence

Implemented in an isolated checkout on 2026-09-08; not integrated, released,
published, deployed, connected to active storage, or externally adopted by this
subtask. Root remains the accountable integrator. SDK PR #5 hold is unchanged.

## Scope

Four-file frozen patch: `src/lib/engine/{chart-adapter.ts,full.ts,portable.ts,portable.test.ts}`.
The source checkout starts at site `d63773a3be2b4d40ff28a1075b9aaa9cb6c10793`
plus the current reviewed, uncommitted rc.5 adoption source. Only these four files
belong to this slice; the copied adoption diff is excluded from the patch.
`identity.json` records the original full adapter, final files, patch, runtime,
and exact rc.5 artifact identities.

`computePortableChart(input, context?)` executes the actual public `natalChart`
exactly once. The same complete native Chart is supplied to the SDK receipt
creator and projected into the existing compact site Chart shape. The snapshot
comes only from validated receipt fields, retaining requested houses even when
the actual system falls back to Whole or is absent. No native Chart is rebuilt
from an abbreviated saved summary, and no second calculation is used.

The shared pure mapper preserves existing `full.ts` synchronous behavior,
caller input identity, and numerical-reference behavior. It has no runtime SDK
or ephemeris import. The optional boundary is not imported by full/math or any
UI/account/storage/server entry. No active C02 saving, export, migration or
remote-account behavior is changed.

## Privacy and historical-time boundaries

The receipt and canonical JSON input snapshot are detached and recursively
frozen; the presentation chart remains mutable, with a separate Date and flags
array. The snapshot uses an ISO string rather than a frozen-but-still-mutable
Date. The envelope uses shallow readonly TypeScript properties plus documented
recursive runtime freezing so existing SDK serialization remains type-safe.

Source spelling, local resolution, reference convention and provenance must be
provided explicitly. An unknown-time 08:30 input remains 08:30; an unknown-time
noon input does not establish a noon convention. The SDK validates and detaches
context after calculation. This is not an atomic entry-time snapshot across
caller-owned getters: an input getter can change context before receipt
creation. A regression documents the timing. Provenance remains unauthenticated
caller assertions, and current Intl/tzdb is never used to reconstruct context.

Errors have one fixed message/code, with no raw error inspection, logging or
cause. Same-realm getters/proxies are not sandboxed. No account, persistent
storage, network request, external publication or production change is involved.

## Tests

`final-focused-test.log`: 80/80 passed on Node 22.23.2, Vitest 3.2.6:

- 21 new boundary cases: actual calculation/receipt object and call counts;
  requested-vs-actual houses; unknown 08:30 and source ISO spelling; missing
  location; canonical defaults and flags; one-read raw getters and getter-induced
  caller mutation; explicit context timing; immutable detached outputs and
  mutable-chart mutation across every numerical branch; source Date/flags/context
  mutation; context accessors/cycles/non-JSON/oversize data; fixed private errors
  including a thrown hostile Proxy; no current Intl or network/storage calls;
  SDK codec round trip; unchanged full adapter references; browser module graphs.
- 53 unchanged engine reference tests, with unchanged fixtures and tolerances.
- 6 installed rc.5 package integration tests, copied with the adoption prerequisite.

`final-typecheck.log`: focused strict TypeScript check passed for all four files.
`final-diff-check.log`: whitespace check passed. `final-runs.json` records exact
commands and exit codes. No complete site test/build/browser/CI or production
claim is made here; the integrator must perform release gates after integration.

